WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.880
We all want to eat
the kinds of foods

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.860
that make us feel
better and live longer.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.920
But there’s so much conflicting
information out there,

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.440
so many nutrition opinions.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.620
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.420
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.120
It’s my job to give you
the information you need

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.520
to make the healthiest
choices possible.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.020
What’s the best way to protect one
of our most important senses?

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.005
We start with the story of two
very important plant pigments

00:00:29.005 --> 00:00:33.171
that help guard against age-
related macular degeneration.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.120
Anyone who has ever got a sunburn knows

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.640
how damaging the UV rays
in sunlight can be.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.060
Imagine what those rays are doing

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.060
to the back of our eyeballs,
our retinas?

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.180
The eye’s designed to take
sunlight and focus it

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.700
like a magnifying glass
into the back of our eyes.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.940
Thankfully we have a layer
of cells in our eye

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.520
called the retinal pigment epithelium

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.640
that supports and protects our
delicate retinal eyesight machinery.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:05.220
This layer builds up yellow plant pigments
from our diet, like zeaxantin,

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.660
which absorbs blue light and protects
the retina from photo-oxidative damage.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.220
The yellowing of our corneas
when we get cataracts

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.460
may actually be our bodies’ defense
mechanism to protect our retinas.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.880
In fact when we go and surgically
remove those cataracts,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.580
our risk of blindness from macular
degeneration shoots up

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.500
since we’ve removed that protection.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.860
Instead of trading one type
of vision loss for another,

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.040
instead of pigmenting the front
of our eye with cataracts,

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.280
better to pigment the back
of eyes with diet.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.960
The pigment in the back of our eye
is entirely of dietary origin,

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.820
thus suggesting that
the most common cause

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.220
of going blind in the Western
world could be delayed

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:47.940
or even averted with appropriate
dietary modification.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.340
Where in our diet do we get it?

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:54.060
Well, the egg industry brags
that eggs are a good source,

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:58.980
but have an egg nearly day, six
eggs a week for three months,

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.260
and the pigmentation in
our eyes barely moves.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:04.920
And these were the high lutein,
free range, certified organic eggs,

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.500
not purchased at the supermarket,
but from a local farm.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.260
Instead of getting phytonutrients

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.300
from the egg that came from the chicken

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.600
that came from the corn and
blades of grass you pecked on,

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.820
what about getting it from the source:

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:21.720
a cup of corn and a half cup
of spinach a day for three months?

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.740
A dramatic boost in
protective eye pigment.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.100
What’s also so neat about
this study is that it went back

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.980
and measured the levels three
months after the study stopped,

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.440
and the levels were still way up here.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.960
So once we build our
macular pigment up

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.320
with a healthy diet, our eyeballs
really try to hold on to it.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.760
So even if we go on vacation

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.520
and end up eating more
iceberg lettuce than spinach,

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.060
our eyes will hold out until we get back.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.320
Yes, eyes can increase zeaxantin
levels in the blood,

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.380
but they also raise bad cholesterol
levels and risk of heart disease,

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.200
therefore an egg yolk based
dietary strategy

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.080
to increase plasma zeaxantin
cannot be recommended.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.320
An alternative, you know, a cholesterol-free
food source is desirable,

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.860
like goji berries for example, which have

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.620
up to 60 times more zeaxantin than eggs.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.920
A modest dose markedly
increases levels in our body.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.180
An inexpensive, effective, safe,
whole foods strategy

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.760
to increase the zeaxantin
in our blood stream.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.740
But we don't need it in our blood.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.360
We need it in our eyes.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.920
So how about a double-blind randomized
placebo-controlled trial?

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.280
To preserve eyesight in the elderly
in traditional Chinese medicine,

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:36.960
people are often prescribed
40 to 100 goji berries a day.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:40.860
But here they just used 15 berries
a day for three months.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:44.100
But still found it could
protect against loss of pigment

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.740
and prevent the buildup of
what’s called soft drusen,

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.380
which is just debris that builds up
in the back of our eye,

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:52.680
both of which are associated with
age-related macular degeneration,

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.040
the leading cause of legal blindness
in older men and women,

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.280
affecting more than 10 million Americans.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.240
Now note they gave the berries
with milk in this study,

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.540
so the butterfat could increase
the absorption of the carotenoid pigments.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:10.800
A healthier way to get the same effect
would be to just eat goji berries

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.306
with nuts or seeds, in other
words, Goji trail mix.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:17.160
In our next story,

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:20.460
kale and collard greens
play a starring role

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.805
in the prevention of glaucoma.

00:04:23.328 --> 00:04:25.560
Glaucoma is the
second leading cause

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:27.240
of legal blindness
in white women,

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.380
but the #1 cause of blindness
in African-American women.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.320
That's one reason researchers
chose a population

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.780
of African-American women
to study the effects

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.260
of fruit and vegetable consumption
on glaucoma risk,

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.060
but the other reason
is because they were

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.880
specifically interested in foods
with the highest concentration

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.480
of those eye-protecting
phytonutrients like zeaxanthin--

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.400
kale and collard greens—

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.300
— but you'd be lucky if you
could find 1 in 10 white people

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.700
eating even a single
serving a month,

00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:00.480
whereas that was a no-brainer
for African Americans.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:02.220
What'd they find?

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.500
Well, as I've stressed
over the years,

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.720
all fruits and vegetables
are not the same.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.840
Whether you ever
ate bananas

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.700
or had one or more
bananas every day

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:12.960
didn't seem to
matter much,

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.540
but eating a couple
oranges every week

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:18.660
was associated with
dramatically lower risk.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:22.020
Not orange juice, though,
you can drink orange juice

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.700
every day and it
didn't seem to matter.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.280
A similar finding with peaches.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.220
Fresh peaches seemed to work
but canned peaches didn't.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.880
Similarly vegetables in
general as a catch-all term

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:33.960
didn't seem to matter.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.080
For example, whether you ate
a green salad twice a week,

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.760
once a week or
zero times a week

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:40.440
didn't seem to matter
when it came to

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.820
reducing glaucoma risk–

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.854
But you know how pitiful
most people's salads are.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:51.000
White people, take note,
as you may need it even more.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:55.620
The lighter our eye color,
the more greens we need to eat.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:59.280
Blue eyes let 100 times
more light through,

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.740
so people with blue
or gray eyes appear

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:03.780
significantly more
vulnerable to damage

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.280
compared to brown or black,

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:08.160
with green and hazel
somewhere in the middle.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:12.300
It's interesting - carrots
appeared to be less protective

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:16.320
in black women compared
to white women.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.500
They suggest it could
be a difference

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.660
in food preparation methods.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:24.180
Perhaps the African
American subjects

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.740
tended to eat
carrots raw,

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.900
limiting the absorption
of certain nutrients,

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.120
while they chopped and prepared
their collard greens

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:32.760
with oil making the nutrients
more bioavailable,

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:35.880
because the absorption of
carotenoid phytonutrients

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.320
depends on the
presence of fat,

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:40.200
which is why I encourage
people to eat nuts or seeds

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.780
with their greens—a little
tahini sauce or something.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:45.960
Why not just take a
zeaxanthin pill?

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:49.800
Well, we don't know
what exactly is in

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.720
these wonderful foods that's
working their wonders

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:55.440
so it may be better to just
recommend folks eat them,

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.670
rather than supplements.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:07:00.060
And in fact, people that take
calcium or iron supplements

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.260
may be doubling, quadrupling,
or septupling

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.820
their odds of glaucoma.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.400
Better to just get
most of our nutrients

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.349
from produce, not pills.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:12.960
Finally today,

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.860
we look at the best dietary
treatments for eye strain.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:21.120
What happens to our eyesight if we sit
in front of a computer all day?

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:25.650
In previous years "the rapid spread of
computers in the home and workplace

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:28.620
has led to an increase in
ocular and visual problems,

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:33.600
including eye discomfort, blurring of distant
objects, eye strain, and visual fatigue,"

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:37.980
so called nearwork-induced transient myopia.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.560
That's when, after staring at
a computer screen for a while,

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.020
you look out the window and
things start out all blurry.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:48.060
That's because our poor little ciliary
muscles pulling at the lenses in our eyes

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:52.380
are locked in this constant state of
contraction to keep that near focus.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:56.820
Over time this can have
long-term adverse consequences.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:08:00.600
Yes, we could waste
4 to 12 minutes an hour

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.160
taking breaks staring out the window,

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:05.160
but what if you've got
nutrition videos to make?

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:10.200
The effects of black currant
intake on video display terminal

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:14.460
work-induced transient refractive
alteration in healthy humans.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:19.080
A double-blind placebo-controlled
crossover study

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.380
finding a significant improvement
in refractive values

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:24.960
and eye strain symptoms
compared to placebo.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.100
Note what passes for currants in the U.S.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:30.960
are actually champagne grape raisins,

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:35.340
not actual black currants,
which were banned in the U.S.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.800
a century ago at the behest
of the lumber industry

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:41.460
for fear that they might spread a plant
disease that affects white pine,

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:43.560
which we hardly even harvest any more.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:48.300
They are, however, currant-ly [cough]
are making a comeback,

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.960
though any anthocyanin-rich berry
might have similar benefits.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:56.040
For example, there was a previous
study done on bilberries.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:59.100
Why didn't I report on it
when it came out?

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:02.460
Because I can't read Japanese.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:07.560
Why not just take
bilberry powder capsules?

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:10.200
Because, as we've seen over and over,

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.740
when you test supplements
you're lucky if they have

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.300
any of what it says on the label.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:19.020
Furthermore, for products actually
containing bilberries at all,

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:22.380
labeling was often uninformative,
misleading or both,

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:25.740
something the herbal supplement
market is infamous for.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.900
The largest study to date found

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:31.320
that it appears most herbal
supplement labels lie.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:31.860
And who wouldn't want to eat this,
rather than this?

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:35.460
It's interesting — bilberries gained
notoriety during World War II

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.940
when it was said that pilots
in the British Royal Air Force

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:42.360
were eating bilberry jam
to improve their night vision.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:48.180
Turns out this may have been a story
concocted to fool the Germans.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:52.140
The real reason the Brits were able
to all the sudden target Nazi bombers

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:54.840
in the middle of the night before
they even made it to the English Channel

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:59.820
was likely not because of bilberries,
but because of a top secret new invention

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:04.839
they needed to keep quiet, called radar.

